1
00:00:01,168 --> 00:00:02,586
Hey, everybody.
Happy Thanksgiving.

2
00:00:02,628 --> 00:00:04,171
No, no, no.
Shh.

3
00:00:04,212 --> 00:00:08,049
Are we keeping Thanksgiving
a secret this year?

4
00:00:08,091 --> 00:00:10,803
No, we're playing this
game I learned at work.

5
00:00:10,845 --> 00:00:13,597
You have to name
all the states
in six minutes.

6
00:00:13,639 --> 00:00:15,933
What? That's like insanely easy.

7
00:00:15,975 --> 00:00:18,435
No, it's a lot harder
than it sounds.

8
00:00:18,477 --> 00:00:22,105
You always forget at least one,
or in some cases, fourteen.

9
00:00:22,147 --> 00:00:25,609
It's a stupid game,
and I wasn't playing
against other people

10
00:00:25,651 --> 00:00:27,402
so, technically,
I didn't lose.

11
00:00:27,444 --> 00:00:29,989
You forgot 14 states?

12
00:00:30,029 --> 00:00:33,241
Nobody cares
about the Dakotas.

13
00:00:33,283 --> 00:00:34,242
( timer dinging )

14
00:00:34,284 --> 00:00:35,494
Oop. Okay, time's up.

15
00:00:35,536 --> 00:00:37,120
All right, I got 48.

16
00:00:37,162 --> 00:00:38,789
That's not bad. Pheebs?

17
00:00:38,831 --> 00:00:40,708
Well, I got tired
of naming states

18
00:00:40,749 --> 00:00:43,126
so I decided to list
the types of celery.

19
00:00:44,879 --> 00:00:48,131
And I have one-- regular celery.

20
00:00:48,173 --> 00:00:50,300
Okay, so Rachel's got 48

21
00:00:50,342 --> 00:00:53,929
and Phoebe has the lead
in... vegetables.

22
00:00:53,971 --> 00:00:55,639
Joey?

23
00:00:55,681 --> 00:00:58,893
Say hello to the new champ
of Chandler's dumb states game.

24
00:00:58,934 --> 00:01:00,936
Wow, how many
do you got?

25
00:01:00,978 --> 00:01:03,146
Fifty-six.

26
00:01:10,445 --> 00:01:14,992
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

27
00:01:15,034 --> 00:01:17,036
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

28
00:01:17,077 --> 00:01:20,163
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

29
00:01:20,205 --> 00:01:24,919
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

30
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:28,213
♪ When it hasn't been your day,
your week, your month ♪

31
00:01:28,255 --> 00:01:30,507
♪ Or even your year ♪

32
00:01:30,549 --> 00:01:33,844
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

33
00:01:33,886 --> 00:01:39,975
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

34
00:01:44,063 --> 00:01:46,481
Hey, how is New England
not a state? Huh?

35
00:01:46,523 --> 00:01:49,484
They have a sports team.

36
00:01:49,526 --> 00:01:52,071
Does South Oregon
have a sports team?

37
00:01:54,113 --> 00:01:55,115
There you go.

38
00:01:56,951 --> 00:01:59,870
How come there's
one extra place setting?

39
00:01:59,912 --> 00:02:01,580
Because you invited
your assistant.

40
00:02:01,622 --> 00:02:02,581
Oh. Right. Sorry.

41
00:02:02,623 --> 00:02:03,582
Tag's not coming.

42
00:02:03,624 --> 00:02:05,250
His girlfriend
came into town

43
00:02:05,292 --> 00:02:07,586
so he's spending
Thanksgiving with her.

44
00:02:07,628 --> 00:02:09,421
Oh, why didn't you tell me?

45
00:02:09,463 --> 00:02:13,174
I made him his own individual
sweet potato stuffed pumpkin.

46
00:02:13,216 --> 00:02:16,095
Oh, well, I was going
to, but then I figured

47
00:02:16,136 --> 00:02:19,098
you know, your food
is so delicious
and perfect

48
00:02:19,138 --> 00:02:22,601
you can't ever have
too many of those
pumpkin things.

49
00:02:22,643 --> 00:02:25,062
You'd think
I wouldn't enjoy that

50
00:02:25,104 --> 00:02:27,940
because it is so fake,
but I still do.

51
00:02:27,982 --> 00:02:30,651
Regular celery.

52
00:02:30,692 --> 00:02:32,027
Oh, I already have that.

53
00:02:32,069 --> 00:02:33,194
Oh...

54
00:02:35,322 --> 00:02:38,909
Done... with time
to spare.

55
00:02:38,951 --> 00:02:41,954
Ooh, this may be
a new world's record.

56
00:02:41,996 --> 00:02:43,872
You know, I hate
to lecture you guys

57
00:02:43,914 --> 00:02:45,332
but it's kind
of disgraceful

58
00:02:45,373 --> 00:02:47,292
that a group
of well-educated adults

59
00:02:47,334 --> 00:02:49,837
and Joey...

60
00:02:49,878 --> 00:02:52,506
can't name all the states.

61
00:02:52,547 --> 00:02:54,049
You ever see a map?

62
00:02:54,091 --> 00:02:57,052
Or one of those round,
colorful things called a globe?

63
00:02:57,094 --> 00:02:58,303
Hmm?

64
00:02:58,345 --> 00:02:59,972
Uh, Magellan?

65
00:03:00,014 --> 00:03:02,432
You got 46 states.

66
00:03:02,474 --> 00:03:03,475
What?

67
00:03:03,517 --> 00:03:04,810
That's impossible.

68
00:03:04,852 --> 00:03:06,436
Forty-six.

69
00:03:06,478 --> 00:03:09,898
Well, who's well educated now,
Mr. I-forgot-ten-states?

70
00:03:11,817 --> 00:03:12,776
I'm out of oven space.

71
00:03:12,818 --> 00:03:14,319
I'm going to go turn on Joey's.

72
00:03:14,361 --> 00:03:15,654
Please watch him.

73
00:03:15,696 --> 00:03:17,196
Do not let Joey eat
any of the food.

74
00:03:17,238 --> 00:03:19,116
I am only one man.

75
00:03:19,158 --> 00:03:20,868
( timer beeping )

76
00:03:20,909 --> 00:03:22,161
Okay, Ross, time is up.

77
00:03:22,201 --> 00:03:23,871
No, just give me
another minute.

78
00:03:23,912 --> 00:03:25,789
Look, Ross, if you don't
know them by now

79
00:03:25,831 --> 00:03:27,290
you will never know them, okay?

80
00:03:27,332 --> 00:03:29,376
That is the beauty
of this game.

81
00:03:29,417 --> 00:03:31,753
It makes you want
to kill yourself.

82
00:03:31,795 --> 00:03:33,088
But th-th-this is crazy.

83
00:03:33,130 --> 00:03:34,673
I can do this.

84
00:03:34,715 --> 00:03:37,676
All right, uh, I bet
I can get all 50 before dinner.

85
00:03:37,718 --> 00:03:40,179
Okay, but if you can't,
no dinner.

86
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:41,763
You're on.

87
00:03:41,805 --> 00:03:43,390
All right.
Don't look at my list, Ross

88
00:03:43,431 --> 00:03:45,642
'cause there's a lot on there
that you don't have.

89
00:03:47,978 --> 00:03:50,480
Hey, did you guys know
that your oven doesn't work?

90
00:03:50,522 --> 00:03:53,525
But the drawer full
of take-out menus
is okay, right?

91
00:03:53,567 --> 00:03:56,028
Ross, I'm going
to use yours, okay?

92
00:03:56,070 --> 00:03:57,696
Shh.

93
00:03:57,738 --> 00:03:59,698
Chandler, give me a hand.

94
00:03:59,740 --> 00:04:01,992
Sure. And, Joey,
do not let Ross look

95
00:04:02,034 --> 00:04:03,326
at any of the maps

96
00:04:03,368 --> 00:04:05,120
or the globe in your apartment.

97
00:04:05,162 --> 00:04:06,329
Don't worry, Chandler.

98
00:04:06,371 --> 00:04:08,289
It's not a globe of
the United States.

99
00:04:15,756 --> 00:04:19,093
Hey, you guys, I'm going
to go out and take a walk.

100
00:04:19,134 --> 00:04:21,178
Phoebe, why is
your bag moving?

101
00:04:21,220 --> 00:04:22,846
Oh. It's not.

102
00:04:22,888 --> 00:04:23,972
Seriously. It's moving.

103
00:04:24,014 --> 00:04:25,265
What the hell's in there?

104
00:04:25,306 --> 00:04:27,601
It's just my knitting,
that's all. Ooh.

105
00:04:33,107 --> 00:04:35,192
Yes, I knit this.

106
00:04:36,818 --> 00:04:39,029
I'm very good.

107
00:04:42,991 --> 00:04:44,492
You know, Ross's
apartment is nice.

108
00:04:44,534 --> 00:04:46,411
How come we don't hang out
here more often?

109
00:04:46,453 --> 00:04:47,621
I don't know.

110
00:04:47,662 --> 00:04:49,206
Maybe because it
smells so weird.

111
00:04:49,248 --> 00:04:50,958
It's like old
pumpkins or something.

112
00:04:50,999 --> 00:04:52,126
That's my pie.

113
00:04:52,167 --> 00:04:54,544
Which smells delicious.

114
00:04:54,586 --> 00:04:55,921
Uh-oh. Uh-oh.

115
00:04:55,963 --> 00:04:57,005
What?

116
00:04:57,047 --> 00:04:59,216
We left Joey alone
with the food.

117
00:04:59,258 --> 00:05:01,093
Yep. Yep. I knew it.

118
00:05:01,135 --> 00:05:05,931
There he is... feeding
stuffing to a dog!

119
00:05:08,308 --> 00:05:11,228
( phone ringing )

120
00:05:11,270 --> 00:05:13,396
Geller-Bing residence.

121
00:05:13,438 --> 00:05:15,899
How can I help?

122
00:05:15,941 --> 00:05:18,193
Phoebe, why is there
a dog in our apartment?

123
00:05:18,235 --> 00:05:19,736
I'm sorry. Who's this?

124
00:05:19,778 --> 00:05:21,196
Phoebe, there's a dog

125
00:05:21,238 --> 00:05:23,406
sitting on my couch.

126
00:05:23,448 --> 00:05:26,660
Tell her I am allergic,
and I will sue.

127
00:05:28,996 --> 00:05:30,413
No, there's no dog here.

128
00:05:30,455 --> 00:05:31,623
Yes, there is.

129
00:05:31,665 --> 00:05:33,583
He's black and white
and shaggy

130
00:05:33,625 --> 00:05:36,170
and he's sitting next to Rachel
and licking Rachel's hand.

131
00:05:36,211 --> 00:05:40,590
Oh, my God, where are you?!

132
00:05:40,632 --> 00:05:41,716
I'll be right there.

133
00:05:41,758 --> 00:05:42,717
( knocking )

134
00:05:42,759 --> 00:05:43,760
( gasping )

135
00:05:43,802 --> 00:05:45,053
They're here already?

136
00:05:45,095 --> 00:05:46,345
How are they doing this?!

137
00:05:51,310 --> 00:05:52,811
Hi, Tag.

138
00:05:52,853 --> 00:05:54,604
What are you doing here?

139
00:05:54,646 --> 00:05:56,064
I, uh, wanted to see
if your offer

140
00:05:56,106 --> 00:05:58,066
to spend Thanksgiving
with you was still good.

141
00:05:58,108 --> 00:06:00,277
Well, sure. Come on in.

142
00:06:00,319 --> 00:06:02,779
Well, what happened
to your girlfriend?

143
00:06:02,821 --> 00:06:05,615
We, uh, kind of broke up
this morning.

144
00:06:05,657 --> 00:06:07,284
Oh, I'm sorry.

145
00:06:07,326 --> 00:06:09,244
Yeah, so she went
back to Ohio.

146
00:06:09,286 --> 00:06:12,331
Ohio! Thank you.

147
00:06:16,001 --> 00:06:18,253
Huh. Where's the dog?

148
00:06:18,295 --> 00:06:20,297
What dog? There's no...
there's no dog here.

149
00:06:20,339 --> 00:06:22,381
Yeah, that dog left.

150
00:06:24,801 --> 00:06:27,804
Phoebe? Phoebe, open up.

151
00:06:27,846 --> 00:06:30,057
Phoebe:
Th-there's no
dog in here.

152
00:06:30,098 --> 00:06:31,099
( barking )

153
00:06:31,141 --> 00:06:32,142
Phoebe, we can hear

154
00:06:32,184 --> 00:06:34,602
the dog barking.

155
00:06:34,644 --> 00:06:36,146
No, that's just
me coughing.

156
00:06:36,188 --> 00:06:37,856
( forced coughing )

157
00:06:37,898 --> 00:06:39,607
( barking )

158
00:06:41,651 --> 00:06:43,904
Oh, good. There you are.

159
00:06:43,945 --> 00:06:47,324
Listen, um, I have
a dog in my room.

160
00:06:47,366 --> 00:06:49,326
What is it doing here?

161
00:06:49,368 --> 00:06:51,870
Well, I'm watching it
for some friends who
went out of town.

162
00:06:51,912 --> 00:06:53,412
Wait.

163
00:06:53,454 --> 00:06:56,166
Hello. My name
is Clunkers.

164
00:06:56,208 --> 00:07:00,212
May I please stay
with you nice people?

165
00:07:00,254 --> 00:07:02,047
Oh, oh, oh, oh...

166
00:07:02,089 --> 00:07:05,175
I wish you could stay here
but Chandler's allergic.

167
00:07:05,217 --> 00:07:07,094
Extremely allergic, okay?

168
00:07:07,135 --> 00:07:11,181
If I am anywhere near a dog
for more than five minutes

169
00:07:11,223 --> 00:07:13,433
my throat will just close up.

170
00:07:13,474 --> 00:07:15,852
That's odd, 'cause this
dog's been living here

171
00:07:15,894 --> 00:07:17,187
for the past three days.

172
00:07:22,234 --> 00:07:25,528
( hoarsely ):
Really?

173
00:07:25,570 --> 00:07:27,739
Chandler, if the dog
has been here that long

174
00:07:27,781 --> 00:07:29,241
and you haven't had
a reaction

175
00:07:29,283 --> 00:07:31,201
maybe you're not allergic
to this dog.

176
00:07:31,243 --> 00:07:32,994
Well, it still has to go, right?

177
00:07:33,036 --> 00:07:34,579
Why?
Why?

178
00:07:34,621 --> 00:07:36,581
Okay, it's, um...

179
00:07:36,623 --> 00:07:39,084
Don't do it!

180
00:07:39,126 --> 00:07:41,378
Don't do what?

181
00:07:41,420 --> 00:07:44,131
I have to. Okay?
It's time.

182
00:07:48,885 --> 00:07:50,637
Okay, I hate dogs.

183
00:07:50,678 --> 00:07:51,763
What?
What?

184
00:07:51,805 --> 00:07:52,764
Are you out
of your mind?

185
00:07:52,806 --> 00:07:54,015
Phoebe:
That's crazy. Why?

186
00:07:54,057 --> 00:07:55,392
Told you.

187
00:07:58,979 --> 00:08:00,397
They are needy.

188
00:08:00,439 --> 00:08:01,898
They are jumpy.

189
00:08:01,940 --> 00:08:05,860
And you can't tell
what they are thinking

190
00:08:05,902 --> 00:08:08,947
and that scares me
a little bit.

191
00:08:08,989 --> 00:08:10,240
You're right,
they are scary.

192
00:08:10,282 --> 00:08:11,491
( screaming )

193
00:08:11,532 --> 00:08:15,536
She just ate a treat
out of my hand!

194
00:08:15,578 --> 00:08:16,871
Wait a minute.

195
00:08:16,913 --> 00:08:18,498
Do you not like
all dogs?

196
00:08:18,539 --> 00:08:20,167
I mean, not
even puppies?

197
00:08:20,208 --> 00:08:21,709
Is there a puppy here?

198
00:08:23,378 --> 00:08:24,587
You don't like puppies?

199
00:08:24,629 --> 00:08:26,381
Okay, you are new.

200
00:08:29,843 --> 00:08:31,428
Look, Chandler,
I told you.

201
00:08:31,470 --> 00:08:34,264
Never tell anyone
about this dog thing.

202
00:08:34,306 --> 00:08:36,933
It's like Ross
not liking ice cream.

203
00:08:38,226 --> 00:08:39,769
You don't like ice cream?

204
00:08:39,811 --> 00:08:42,605
It's too cold!

205
00:08:42,647 --> 00:08:45,942
Okay, it's just that dogs
make me a little uncomfortable.

206
00:08:45,984 --> 00:08:48,487
Hurts my teeth.

207
00:08:48,528 --> 00:08:50,238
And I don't want to say this

208
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:53,116
and I don't want you guys
to hate me, but, uh...

209
00:08:53,158 --> 00:08:56,370
I don't think I can be
around that dog anymore, okay?

210
00:08:56,411 --> 00:08:58,663
So either the dog goes,
or I go. Huh.

211
00:09:04,252 --> 00:09:07,005
Oh, my God!

212
00:09:09,924 --> 00:09:12,969
How can I not get this?

213
00:09:13,011 --> 00:09:14,721
I'm a college professor.

214
00:09:14,762 --> 00:09:16,681
I got 1450 on my S.A.T.s.

215
00:09:16,723 --> 00:09:18,350
1250.

216
00:09:18,392 --> 00:09:21,769
Damn. I forgot you were here.

217
00:09:21,811 --> 00:09:24,439
All right, we're going
to take Clunkers to Ross's.

218
00:09:24,481 --> 00:09:26,191
We'll be back
in a minute.

219
00:09:26,233 --> 00:09:27,901
Oh, wait. Before you guys go,
can I just ask you a question?

220
00:09:27,942 --> 00:09:29,236
Yeah.

221
00:09:29,277 --> 00:09:30,904
Um, when a guy breaks up
with his girlfriend

222
00:09:30,945 --> 00:09:33,907
what is an appropriate amount
of time to wait

223
00:09:33,948 --> 00:09:35,200
before you make a move?

224
00:09:35,242 --> 00:09:37,118
Oh, I'd say
about a month.

225
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:39,371
Really? I'd say
three to four.

226
00:09:39,413 --> 00:09:40,497
Half hour.

227
00:09:43,708 --> 00:09:46,336
Interesting.

228
00:09:46,378 --> 00:09:48,963
When it's your assistant,
I would say never.

229
00:09:49,005 --> 00:09:52,717
Rach, the big question is,
does he like you? Right?

230
00:09:52,759 --> 00:09:56,930
Because if he doesn't like you,
this is all a moo point.

231
00:09:56,971 --> 00:10:01,268
Huh. A "moo" point?

232
00:10:02,810 --> 00:10:05,688
Yeah. It's like
a cow's opinion.

233
00:10:05,730 --> 00:10:09,317
You know, it just
doesn't matter.

234
00:10:11,861 --> 00:10:13,321
It's moo.

235
00:10:19,119 --> 00:10:21,746
Have I been living
with him for too long

236
00:10:21,788 --> 00:10:23,831
or did that all
just make sense?

237
00:10:23,873 --> 00:10:26,167
Please don't listen
to Joey.

238
00:10:26,209 --> 00:10:28,086
Would you look at him?

239
00:10:28,128 --> 00:10:30,171
He's obviously
depressed.

240
00:10:30,213 --> 00:10:31,465
He's away from his family.

241
00:10:31,506 --> 00:10:33,007
He's spending Thanksgiving
with strangers.

242
00:10:33,049 --> 00:10:35,218
What he needs right now
is for you to be his friend.

243
00:10:35,260 --> 00:10:36,219
Oh, you're right.

244
00:10:36,261 --> 00:10:37,345
I'm sorry. Thank you.

245
00:10:37,387 --> 00:10:39,222
Okay, that's what
I'm going to do.

246
00:10:39,264 --> 00:10:40,932
Fine. Take their advice.

247
00:10:40,974 --> 00:10:42,767
No one ever listens to me.

248
00:10:42,809 --> 00:10:44,936
When the package
is this pretty

249
00:10:44,978 --> 00:10:47,481
no one cares what's inside.

250
00:10:52,569 --> 00:10:54,154
Hey.

251
00:10:54,195 --> 00:10:55,447
Hey.

252
00:10:55,489 --> 00:10:56,823
How you holding up?

253
00:10:56,864 --> 00:10:58,450
Not bad.

254
00:10:58,492 --> 00:11:01,286
Yeah? I'm sorry
about your girlfriend.

255
00:11:01,328 --> 00:11:02,996
Thanks.

256
00:11:03,037 --> 00:11:05,915
So were you guys together
a long time?

257
00:11:05,957 --> 00:11:07,459
A year, on and off.

258
00:11:07,501 --> 00:11:10,003
I kind of thought
we'd end up together.

259
00:11:10,044 --> 00:11:11,129
I don't anymore.

260
00:11:11,171 --> 00:11:12,297
Now that she
broke up with you?

261
00:11:12,339 --> 00:11:14,757
Yeah.
Yeah.

262
00:11:14,799 --> 00:11:15,883
Hmm...

263
00:11:15,925 --> 00:11:17,969
It's weird. I always
used to assume

264
00:11:18,011 --> 00:11:19,513
that I would
meet someone

265
00:11:19,554 --> 00:11:21,389
and fall in love
and be happy

266
00:11:21,431 --> 00:11:23,224
and that all that
was just a given.

267
00:11:23,266 --> 00:11:25,644
But lately, it's like
what if it's not?

268
00:11:25,684 --> 00:11:27,479
Do you ever have
that feeling?

269
00:11:27,521 --> 00:11:29,022
No.

270
00:11:29,063 --> 00:11:31,149
Yeah.

271
00:11:31,191 --> 00:11:33,234
All the time. Constantly.

272
00:11:33,276 --> 00:11:34,653
It's terrifying.

273
00:11:34,693 --> 00:11:38,365
But you know, I figure,
it has to work out.

274
00:11:38,406 --> 00:11:40,325
Why?

275
00:11:40,367 --> 00:11:43,161
Because it has to.

276
00:11:43,203 --> 00:11:45,704
You really have all
the answers, don't you?

277
00:11:45,746 --> 00:11:48,583
Yeah. No, I do.
I really do.

278
00:11:48,625 --> 00:11:50,418
Hey, thanks for
talking to me.

279
00:11:50,460 --> 00:11:52,629
Come on, what are bosses for?

280
00:11:52,671 --> 00:11:54,130
Hug it out.

281
00:11:56,341 --> 00:11:58,134
All right, he
likes you back.

282
00:12:00,387 --> 00:12:03,640
Huh? Told you
you should go for it.

283
00:12:03,682 --> 00:12:05,099
What?

284
00:12:09,103 --> 00:12:11,398
Street noise drown
any of that out?

285
00:12:12,857 --> 00:12:15,193
No? All right,
I'll see you later. Okay.

286
00:12:19,780 --> 00:12:21,199
What did Joey say?

287
00:12:21,241 --> 00:12:22,701
I like you back?

288
00:12:22,741 --> 00:12:25,828
Um, well, you... see...

289
00:12:25,870 --> 00:12:29,374
Joey knows that I'm very...

290
00:12:29,416 --> 00:12:32,293
insecure about my back

291
00:12:32,335 --> 00:12:35,171
and... you were
hugging me

292
00:12:35,213 --> 00:12:38,550
so obviously
you are not
repulsed by it.

293
00:12:38,592 --> 00:12:40,009
Yeah!

294
00:12:40,051 --> 00:12:41,052
Wait a minute.

295
00:12:41,094 --> 00:12:43,221
That doesn't make any sense.

296
00:12:43,263 --> 00:12:45,181
No?

297
00:12:46,182 --> 00:12:48,184
All right.

298
00:12:48,226 --> 00:12:50,144
Here's the truth.

299
00:12:50,186 --> 00:12:51,979
Um... Joey said
what he said

300
00:12:52,021 --> 00:12:53,523
because, um...

301
00:12:55,442 --> 00:12:57,360
I'm attracted to you.

302
00:12:58,403 --> 00:12:59,904
Wow.

303
00:12:59,946 --> 00:13:01,489
Yeah, I admit it.

304
00:13:01,531 --> 00:13:03,575
I have a crush on you

305
00:13:03,617 --> 00:13:05,619
and, uh... and I know
that's crazy

306
00:13:05,660 --> 00:13:07,078
because we work together

307
00:13:07,120 --> 00:13:08,913
and nothing could
ever happen

308
00:13:08,955 --> 00:13:11,165
and the last thing
I wanted to do

309
00:13:11,207 --> 00:13:12,542
is to freak you out

310
00:13:12,584 --> 00:13:14,711
or make you feel
uncomfortable.

311
00:13:14,753 --> 00:13:17,088
Which is why it
would be really great

312
00:13:17,130 --> 00:13:19,591
if you said something
right about now.

313
00:13:19,633 --> 00:13:20,675
Oh, my God.

314
00:13:20,717 --> 00:13:22,343
Those guys are
stealing my car.

315
00:13:22,385 --> 00:13:23,344
What?

316
00:13:23,386 --> 00:13:24,429
Right there!

317
00:13:24,471 --> 00:13:25,597
That's my car!

318
00:13:25,639 --> 00:13:26,598
Oh...

319
00:13:26,640 --> 00:13:27,932
Hey!

320
00:13:27,974 --> 00:13:29,643
Okay, well, that's
going to take one minute.

321
00:13:29,684 --> 00:13:30,893
Do you have
anything else

322
00:13:30,935 --> 00:13:32,437
you want to get
off your chest?

323
00:13:32,479 --> 00:13:33,563
I can't believe this.

324
00:13:33,605 --> 00:13:34,855
We still have time
to talk.

325
00:13:34,897 --> 00:13:37,066
And they're not even
in the car yet.

326
00:13:37,108 --> 00:13:40,403
Oh, look, there they go. Okay.

327
00:13:41,446 --> 00:13:44,823
Okay, Phoebe, we should
probably go back now.

328
00:13:44,865 --> 00:13:46,909
( high-pitched voice ):
Please don't leave me.

329
00:13:46,951 --> 00:13:47,910
I'll be lonely.

330
00:13:47,952 --> 00:13:49,370
Stop it.

331
00:13:49,412 --> 00:13:50,829
Stop.

332
00:13:50,871 --> 00:13:52,165
Okay, let's go.

333
00:13:52,206 --> 00:13:53,874
We can be strong.

334
00:13:53,916 --> 00:13:55,001
Yeah, okay.

335
00:13:55,042 --> 00:13:57,671
( whimpering )

336
00:13:57,712 --> 00:13:59,506
Oh, my God,
did you hear that?

337
00:13:59,547 --> 00:14:00,507
She said "Monica!"

338
00:14:00,548 --> 00:14:02,383
Oh, I can't leave her.

339
00:14:02,425 --> 00:14:04,135
You know,
if you want

340
00:14:04,177 --> 00:14:07,430
we could sneak the dog back in
and Chandler wouldn't even know.

341
00:14:07,472 --> 00:14:08,682
That's not going to work.

342
00:14:08,723 --> 00:14:10,016
I've had that
dog there

343
00:14:10,057 --> 00:14:12,352
for three days
and Chandler had no idea.

344
00:14:12,393 --> 00:14:13,687
He's not so smart...

345
00:14:13,728 --> 00:14:14,853
Hey.

346
00:14:14,895 --> 00:14:16,523
I didn't know either.

347
00:14:16,564 --> 00:14:18,316
Yeah, but you kind of knew

348
00:14:18,358 --> 00:14:21,027
that something was going on,
didn't you?

349
00:14:21,068 --> 00:14:22,987
Yeah, I knew.

350
00:14:28,409 --> 00:14:30,161
Where's Chandler?

351
00:14:30,995 --> 00:14:32,079
Here I am.

352
00:14:32,121 --> 00:14:33,998
Wash your hands!

353
00:14:35,583 --> 00:14:37,960
How did you know?

354
00:14:41,964 --> 00:14:44,676
Hey, what's she
doing back here?

355
00:14:44,718 --> 00:14:45,885
Relax, Ross.

356
00:14:45,926 --> 00:14:47,595
She's not made of ice cream.

357
00:14:47,637 --> 00:14:50,264
Hey, look, Phoebe,
I laid out the states
geographically.

358
00:14:50,306 --> 00:14:52,350
We don't really have time
for this right now.

359
00:14:52,392 --> 00:14:55,353
We have to keep Chandler
away from my bedroom.

360
00:14:55,395 --> 00:14:57,856
Yeah, but look
what I did...

361
00:14:57,938 --> 00:15:00,650
See? This is exactly
what we do not have time for.

362
00:15:02,736 --> 00:15:05,238
Where's Monica?

363
00:15:05,279 --> 00:15:06,573
In Phoebe's room.

364
00:15:06,614 --> 00:15:07,948
You can't go in there.

365
00:15:07,990 --> 00:15:08,991
Why not?

366
00:15:09,033 --> 00:15:10,368
( dog whimpering )

367
00:15:11,870 --> 00:15:13,913
Monica's crying.

368
00:15:13,954 --> 00:15:19,252
She's very upset
about this whole
Clunkers thing.

369
00:15:19,293 --> 00:15:21,087
Well, I... I should
go in there.

370
00:15:21,128 --> 00:15:24,006
No. No. No, she
doesn't want

371
00:15:24,048 --> 00:15:26,342
to see you right now.

372
00:15:26,384 --> 00:15:28,052
Why not?

373
00:15:28,094 --> 00:15:31,097
Because you sent
away the dog.

374
00:15:31,138 --> 00:15:32,432
That's ridiculous.

375
00:15:32,473 --> 00:15:33,974
Oh, is it?
Is it?!

376
00:15:35,643 --> 00:15:38,646
Look, when Monica
and I were kids

377
00:15:38,688 --> 00:15:40,981
we had a dog named Rover

378
00:15:41,023 --> 00:15:46,446
and, uh, one day my dad
decides he doesn't like dogs

379
00:15:46,487 --> 00:15:50,450
so Monica and her
friend... Phyllis...

380
00:15:50,491 --> 00:15:51,826
take away the dog

381
00:15:51,868 --> 00:15:55,371
and that was the last time
we ever saw him.

382
00:15:55,413 --> 00:15:58,416
Don't you see?
This is just like that

383
00:15:58,458 --> 00:16:01,085
only with
a few details changed.

384
00:16:02,295 --> 00:16:04,297
( door opens )

385
00:16:04,338 --> 00:16:05,924
Okay, I'm in my sweatpants.

386
00:16:05,964 --> 00:16:07,717
Bring on the food.

387
00:16:11,846 --> 00:16:12,806
What's the matter?

388
00:16:12,847 --> 00:16:14,390
Monica is all upset

389
00:16:14,432 --> 00:16:16,810
because I sent Clunkers away.

390
00:16:16,851 --> 00:16:18,144
So? Bring the dog back.

391
00:16:18,185 --> 00:16:19,186
You're a hero.

392
00:16:19,228 --> 00:16:20,647
Yeah, I can be a hero.

393
00:16:20,688 --> 00:16:21,815
I could do that.

394
00:16:21,856 --> 00:16:23,274
I could... I could do...

395
00:16:23,316 --> 00:16:25,652
W-what if it attacks me?

396
00:16:25,693 --> 00:16:29,071
Chandler, it's like
a big gerbil.

397
00:16:30,865 --> 00:16:33,159
And that doesn't
scare you?

398
00:16:37,747 --> 00:16:40,207
Ross, you need some help?

399
00:16:40,249 --> 00:16:41,375
From you?

400
00:16:41,417 --> 00:16:42,877
( chuckles, sobs )

401
00:16:42,919 --> 00:16:45,755
( voice breaking ):
Yes, please.

402
00:16:50,176 --> 00:16:52,762
First of all... Utah?

403
00:16:52,804 --> 00:16:55,849
Dude, you can't just
make stuff up.

404
00:17:01,771 --> 00:17:04,440
I hate America!

405
00:17:04,482 --> 00:17:07,610
When I finish this game,
I swear I am moving.

406
00:17:07,652 --> 00:17:08,778
Mmm.

407
00:17:08,820 --> 00:17:11,197
Joey:
Hey.

408
00:17:11,238 --> 00:17:13,199
Tag still talking
to the police?

409
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:15,994
Yeah. Oh, damn it!
Why did I open my mouth?

410
00:17:16,034 --> 00:17:18,162
( whining ):
"I have a crush on you."

411
00:17:18,204 --> 00:17:19,539
"I'm attracted to you."

412
00:17:19,580 --> 00:17:21,290
I know that
I freaked him out.

413
00:17:21,332 --> 00:17:24,377
If you said it like that,
you probably did, yeah.

414
00:17:25,712 --> 00:17:27,547
Hey, is Chandler here?

415
00:17:27,588 --> 00:17:30,383
Uh, no. No, he went for a walk.

416
00:17:30,424 --> 00:17:33,052
Okay, well, you cannot tell him,
but look who's back!

417
00:17:33,093 --> 00:17:34,345
( Rachel gasps )

418
00:17:34,387 --> 00:17:35,889
Oh! Hi!

419
00:17:35,930 --> 00:17:37,223
No, no, no,
no-no-no-no.

420
00:17:37,264 --> 00:17:38,474
He went over to Ross's

421
00:17:38,516 --> 00:17:39,976
to bring the dog
back here.

422
00:17:40,018 --> 00:17:42,937
Oh, no! The dog's
not going to be there.

423
00:17:44,772 --> 00:17:45,940
You think?

424
00:17:50,277 --> 00:17:51,612
Hi, honey.

425
00:17:51,654 --> 00:17:54,782
Please, please, please
don't be mad at me.

426
00:17:54,824 --> 00:17:56,283
What? Wh-why would...

427
00:17:56,325 --> 00:17:57,410
Shh. Wait and see.

428
00:17:57,451 --> 00:18:00,079
Maybe we will,
maybe we won't.

429
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:02,415
Okay, I went over
to Ross's apartment

430
00:18:02,456 --> 00:18:04,500
to bring back Clunkers,
you know

431
00:18:04,542 --> 00:18:06,920
for you, and, uh,
I left the door open

432
00:18:06,961 --> 00:18:08,922
and she must have...
gotten out

433
00:18:08,963 --> 00:18:11,632
and I looked everywhere

434
00:18:11,674 --> 00:18:14,010
all over the apartment,
including the roof

435
00:18:14,052 --> 00:18:16,387
which, FYI, Ross,
one of your neighbors?

436
00:18:16,429 --> 00:18:17,805
Growing weed.

437
00:18:19,515 --> 00:18:21,267
I couldn't find him

438
00:18:21,308 --> 00:18:27,774
and I am so, so, so sorry,
but... I do know

439
00:18:27,815 --> 00:18:30,985
where we can all go
ease the pain.

440
00:18:32,570 --> 00:18:33,780
We have good news.

441
00:18:33,821 --> 00:18:34,864
Look who's back.

442
00:18:34,906 --> 00:18:36,866
Hey!

443
00:18:36,908 --> 00:18:38,785
Clunkers!
Oh, my God!

444
00:18:38,826 --> 00:18:39,827
Monica:
That's right.

445
00:18:39,869 --> 00:18:41,662
She came back
all by herself.

446
00:18:41,704 --> 00:18:44,624
It's a Thanksgiving
miracle!

447
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:48,878
It is so good to see you!

448
00:18:48,920 --> 00:18:51,505
Yeah, she came all the way
back from Ross's building.

449
00:18:51,547 --> 00:18:54,174
Oh, the things
she must have seen!

450
00:18:55,468 --> 00:18:57,136
And she climbed up
the fire escape

451
00:18:57,177 --> 00:18:59,931
and she tapped on the window
with her teeny little paw

452
00:18:59,973 --> 00:19:01,515
and then we ran
to let her in.

453
00:19:03,476 --> 00:19:06,312
I went too far, didn't I?

454
00:19:06,353 --> 00:19:08,481
When should I have stopped?

455
00:19:13,111 --> 00:19:14,946
Okay, maybe
this is so hard

456
00:19:14,988 --> 00:19:18,116
because there aren't 50 states.

457
00:19:19,826 --> 00:19:21,077
Let me tell you something--

458
00:19:21,119 --> 00:19:23,370
I had 49 states

459
00:19:23,412 --> 00:19:26,916
and there are no more!

460
00:19:26,958 --> 00:19:30,003
Now, I think I should
be able to eat something.

461
00:19:30,044 --> 00:19:32,212
It's up to you.

462
00:19:32,254 --> 00:19:35,341
( cries )

463
00:19:36,843 --> 00:19:38,803
Oh, hi.
How are you doing?

464
00:19:38,845 --> 00:19:40,013
I'm okay.

465
00:19:40,054 --> 00:19:41,514
I got to go down
to the police station

466
00:19:41,555 --> 00:19:42,682
and look at mug shots.

467
00:19:42,723 --> 00:19:44,934
Thanks for having me
over, you guys.

468
00:19:44,976 --> 00:19:47,227
Tag, you're going?

469
00:19:47,269 --> 00:19:48,646
We didn't, uh...

470
00:19:48,688 --> 00:19:50,230
We didn't even get
a chance to talk.

471
00:19:50,272 --> 00:19:52,650
So, where did you say
you were from again?

472
00:19:52,692 --> 00:19:53,567
Colorado.

473
00:19:53,609 --> 00:19:55,235
Aw, what good are you?

474
00:20:01,367 --> 00:20:03,995
Look, um, I think we
should talk about

475
00:20:04,037 --> 00:20:05,538
what happened
on the terrace.

476
00:20:05,579 --> 00:20:07,081
Okay.

477
00:20:07,123 --> 00:20:08,916
Uh, I never should've
said what I said.

478
00:20:08,958 --> 00:20:11,044
You know what, it just
doesn't matter how I feel.

479
00:20:11,085 --> 00:20:13,504
We work together, so
nothing could really

480
00:20:13,546 --> 00:20:15,464
ever happen between us.

481
00:20:15,506 --> 00:20:16,799
And what I would love

482
00:20:16,841 --> 00:20:18,216
is just to go
to work on Monday

483
00:20:18,258 --> 00:20:20,845
and never talk
about this again.

484
00:20:20,887 --> 00:20:24,390
Okay, big day Monday,
lots to do.

485
00:20:24,431 --> 00:20:26,350
So, we okay?

486
00:20:26,392 --> 00:20:28,728
Um, I'm not.

487
00:20:28,769 --> 00:20:30,563
Oh, God, I knew it.
I freaked you out.

488
00:20:30,604 --> 00:20:32,314
No, you didn't.

489
00:20:32,356 --> 00:20:34,025
The only thing
that freaked me out

490
00:20:34,067 --> 00:20:36,736
was you saying that nothing
could ever happen between us.

491
00:20:36,777 --> 00:20:38,988
Really?

492
00:20:39,030 --> 00:20:40,239
Yeah.

493
00:20:40,280 --> 00:20:43,409
So please don't fire me
for doing this.

494
00:20:53,711 --> 00:20:55,254
Okay, well,
that's one less thing

495
00:20:55,295 --> 00:20:56,672
we have to do on Monday.

496
00:21:02,302 --> 00:21:03,303
( knocking on door )

497
00:21:17,651 --> 00:21:19,361
Delaware.

498
00:21:21,948 --> 00:21:25,076
( cries ):
Delaware.

499
00:21:25,118 --> 00:21:26,284
All right.

500
00:21:26,326 --> 00:21:28,788
I want my turkey now.

501
00:21:28,829 --> 00:21:31,040
You got it.

502
00:21:35,419 --> 00:21:38,505
You got Nevada twice.

503
00:21:41,175 --> 00:21:42,551
I know.

504
00:21:46,680 --> 00:21:51,227
[Captioned by
The Caption Center
WGBH Educational Foundation]

